Z||000000||GT Bastard||12-04-2000||01:52 AM||||Is it true that 4th gen seats lose 1.5 inches?  If so, I'm gonna screw this seat deal I've got in the works because I don't want to be sitting any closer to the steering wheel. thanks for any info...||||reg||5
Z||000001||horseman||12-04-2000||10:12 AM||||Keep us posted GTB,<BR>I am also considering the switch. Like you, I don't want to lose any leg room with that clutch pedal there.(6'3")||||reg||12
Z||000002||Will||12-04-2000||11:15 AM||||I fully understand the desire to stay cheap, but has anyone looked into C5 Vette seats? They are very low and have all kinds of power adjustments.<BR>     Is the same true of the fourth gen F-body seats? I haven't seen any yet.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula 18||12-04-2000||06:43 PM||||It is ture and false...<P>If you use the 4th Gen seat tracks you will lose about 1.5 inches (you also have to grind out a little of the mouting holes)but if you use your fiero seat tracks you wont lose any head room but you will lose that neat tilt (like a rocking chair) feature. You'll also have to find some where to put that pump for air adjust lumbar. <P>I have seats out of a Sunbird Turbo coupe in my Formula. They that adjustable lumar and inflatable bolsters. I had to put them on the fireo tracks though because I lost a lot of head room. Like 4 inches on their tracks. <BR>When I replace my center console I'll try to put the pump in there some where. It isn't very big but there isn't much room in there either. If Not maybe I'll just mount it behind the seats next to my amp. <P>One more note. Make sure you get the wiring harness and the tube to go between seats. You'll have to add about 2 feet to them also. <P>Hope this helps<BR><P>------------------<BR>Brian<BR> -88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000004||the need for speed||12-05-2000||12:45 AM||||what is a 4th gen seat? and what type of car can you get them out of any pic's||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJRice||12-05-2000||09:57 AM||||Check out this thread:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20000815-1-001006.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000002/HTML/20000815-1-001006.html</A> <P>F-body seats are seats from the late model Camaro/Firebirds.  I did this swap last year and it is discussed a bit in that thread.  <P>As was mentioned, if you use the fiero seat rails you wont notice much of a difference except for some of the extra adjustments that these new seats have.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
